  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at The Pinhook in Durham, North Carolina, on Saturday, November 22, 2025, delivering a 92-minute set that spans their extensive catalog [1][2]. The recording, taped and transferred by Liz Hamilton, is the only available audio for this date and captures all 21 songs [1]. The setlist begins with “Going Invisible 2” from *In League with Dragons* and “Psalms 40:2” from *The Life of the World to Come*, both of which had not been played in over two years [1][2]. The band revisited “Against Pollution” and “White Cedar,” each absent from the stage for roughly three years, before moving into “Transcendental Youth” and “Cotton” [1][2]. Notable rarities include “Shave My Eyebrows,” an unreleased track with only three archived performances, and “The Last Limit of Bhakti,” which has appeared in just seven shows [1][2]. The set also features “Peru,” the earliest archived recording of that song, alongside “Carmen Cicero,” another unreleased piece [1][2]. The encore includes “Dance Music” from *The Sunset Tree* and “Solidarity Forever,” a rare anthem with only ten archived performances [1][2]. This show is the 443rd in the archive’s collection for the band, following a performance at Motorco on November 6, 2025 [2]. The lineup offers a balanced mix of deep cuts and recent material, providing a comprehensive snapshot of the band’s current musical direction [1][2].",
